<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puente la Reina</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gares</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puente la Reina is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> on the river Arga, where the main pilgrim routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-de-compostela">Santiago de Compostela</a> from Roncesvalles and from Somport join. It takes its name from the six-arched Romanesque bridge built for pilgrims in the eleventh century, traditionally at the order of a queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a>. The town grew around the bridge as a settlement of Frankish traders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puente-la-reina.jpg" alt="Puente la Reina" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Piotr Tysarczyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puente_la_reina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
